WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.502
-Guys, it is
the end of the week.

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.503
That's usually when I catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:06.439
You know, I check my in-box,
I return some e-mails,

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.107
and, of course,
I send out thank-you notes.

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:10.709
And I was running a bit
behind today, so I thought,

00:00:10.709 --> 00:00:12.312
if you guys wouldn't mind,
I'd just like to write out

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:13.746
my weekly thank-you notes
right now.

00:00:13.746 --> 00:00:16.215
Is that cool with you guys?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:17.916
The best. Thank you, thank you.

00:00:17.916 --> 00:00:18.985
James, can I get some

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.619
thank-you-note-writing
music, please?

00:00:20.619 --> 00:00:23.890
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.992
That's perfect.
That is the perfect music.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.927
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:30.363
-Gosh, he's --
-Wow.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.397
-Wow.

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:33.666
Hold it. Hold it.
Hang in there, bud.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.902
Hold it. Hold it.
[ Drumroll ]

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.603
Hold it. Not yet.

00:00:37.603 --> 00:00:39.439
Hold it.

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:40.973
That's it. You broke the record.
There you go.

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:42.074
That's it. You did it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:45.145
Pretty good. Not bad.

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:48.047
[ Laughs ]

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:49.249
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:51.651
Thank you, Milk Crate Challenge,

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.819
for raising a lot of
questions, but mainly,

00:00:53.819 --> 00:00:57.557
how do so many people
have access to 49 milk crates?

00:00:57.557 --> 00:01:01.761
Where are they getting these?

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:04.897
-Great idea.

00:01:04.897 --> 00:01:06.165
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:09.401
-Thank you, "Candyman,"
for being the only time

00:01:09.401 --> 00:01:11.404
I have to say
someone's name five times,

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:16.042
besides when I'm trying to
get Alexa's attention.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.711
Alexa, stop.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:23.516
That's the second time
I said the C-word.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.618
I'm not doing it anymore.
-What's that?

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.987
-No, I'm not saying that name.
-Oh. Yeah, don't say it.

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:31.357
-Even if -- I know it's fake,
but just why?

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:33.159
Why put it out there?
-No, don't put it out there.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.794
-I'm not going to
put it out there.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.163
-Don't even play Sammy Davis Jr.
version of it.

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:40.699
-[ As Davis ]
♪ Who can take the sunrise ♪

00:01:40.699 --> 00:01:44.570
♪ Sprinkle it with dew ♪

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:47.974
♪ Da-da-da-da,
to make a miracle or two ♪

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:51.110
♪ The [clears throat] can ♪

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.646
-♪ Oh, Jeff Bezos can ♪

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.682
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.384 --> 00:02:00.786
[ Soft music playing ]

00:02:00.786 --> 00:02:03.222
-Thank you, Krispy Kreme,
upping their

00:02:03.222 --> 00:02:05.290
"free doughnut if you're
vaccinated" campaign

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:07.593
to two free doughnuts

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:09.762
or, as that one guy
on Facebook put it,

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:12.165
"I'm holding out for
a full dozen."

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:20.339
[ Soft music playing ]

00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:23.209
Thank you,
giving plants as a gift,

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.043
for being a fun way of
telling your friend,

00:02:25.043 --> 00:02:27.213
"Here, you kill this."

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.852
With a plant. I don't know.

00:02:34.219 --> 00:02:35.487
[ Soft music playing ]

00:02:35.487 --> 00:02:38.390
Thank you,
automatic minivan doors,

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:40.459
for making me feel like
I'm entering a spaceship,

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:43.229
instead of my 2012 Kia Sedona.

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:45.498
Wow!

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:51.270
[ Soft music playing ]

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:54.273
Thank you, St. Louis arch,
for looking like

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:57.510
the Washington Monument
doing downward-facing dog.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:02.815
A little yoga ref.
-A little yoga ref.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.449
What's up, Peloton?

00:03:04.449 --> 00:03:05.885
[ Soft music playing ]

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:10.355
-Thank you, ascots, for just
being ties worn exclusively by

00:03:10.355 --> 00:03:15.795
guys who challenge each other
to hot-air-balloon races.

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:17.896
Too specific.

00:03:17.896 --> 00:03:21.134
-Very specific.
-That's a specific joke, yeah.

00:03:23.669 --> 00:03:24.770
[ Soft music playing ]

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:27.506
Thank you,
coin-operated binoculars,

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:31.544
for charging me 50 cents to say,
"Oh, yeah, I see it."

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:32.879
Oh.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.582
Yeah.

00:03:39.017 --> 00:03:40.386
[ Soft music playing ]

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:43.422
Thank you, bathrobes,
for being the official wardrobe

00:03:43.422 --> 00:03:47.794
of both fancy hotel guests and
biggest neighborhood dirtbags.

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:55.501
"What are you up to?
I'm waiting for the dozen."

00:03:56.602 --> 00:03:57.970
[ Soft music playing ]

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:01.640
-Thank you, sofa beds,
for managing to be bad at both.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:02.875
Yeah, there you go.

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.210
There you have it.
Those are our "Thank You Notes."

